{"title":"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><dl><dd><i>The following problem is from the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems\">2004 AMC 12A #8</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_10A_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2004 AMC 10A Problems/Problem 9\">2004 AMC 10A #9</a>, so those problems redirect to this page.</i></dd></dl>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4_(coordbash)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4 (coordbash)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Solution_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Solution_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 6</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#See_also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the overlapping <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Triangle\" title=\"Triangle\">triangles</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/8/1f828f10cad9235a2c72c34369f5fd4a1179e579.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABC}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/5/245ff420d808b2e09a77194551ff12dbfda05a19.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ABE}$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> sharing common <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Edge\" title=\"Edge\"> side</a> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/8/068cc77328b74134c841e0f31b4fa2428d394477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{EAB}$\" width=\"55\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/d/0/0d089768b09c8f192985935b4efd1d34ab6094ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle{ABC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"57\" height=\"14\" /> are <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Right_angle\" title=\"Right angle\">right angles</a>, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b44beb78e8be18179bfb7fe6b3424e7fb1aef32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB=4$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/4/2a4826138756e48059393331c30916b2b06430cf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC=6$\" width=\"61\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/8/8982a7982c7df8159c047c172a2b90e531ee3865.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE=8$\" width=\"61\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> intersect at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. What is the difference between the areas of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/c/a/acad5629f89ba033c79d7d59d7c0605d2a5cac48.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{ADE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"62\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/8/738998ea6564224ed451aa403ba88be4a5cd47fc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle{BDC}$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" />? \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/7/d/37d48968371e6d998d5b4c40c47c99005f414ab9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] size(150); defaultpen(linewidth(0.4)); //Variable Declarations pair A, B, C, D, E;  //Variable Definitions A=(0, 0); B=(4, 0); C=(4, 6); E=(0, 8); D=extension(A,C,B,E);  //Initial Diagram draw(A--B--C--A--E--B); label(&quot;$A$&quot;,A,SW); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,B,SE); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,C,NE); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,D,3N); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,E,NW);  //Side labels label(&quot;$4$&quot;,A--B,S); label(&quot;$8$&quot;,A--E,W); label(&quot;$6$&quot;,B--C,ENE); [/asy]\" width=\"152\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/e/1eec0d175928e5a1f77fa50f166f575625ad9fcc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm {(A)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\mathrm {(B)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\mathrm {(C)}\\ 5 \\qquad \\mathrm {(D)}\\ 8 \\qquad \\mathrm {(E)}\\ 9 \\qquad$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"342\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Looking, we see that the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/e/f1ef7b202f1e5573fc600ee2a6bdcc6ab31b0de8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle EBA]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> is 16 and the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/8/2/d82a190a5b7c9859b720674a202e4946b0254099.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ABC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"71\" height=\"20\" /> is 12. Set the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c42fa89302916d03f22d1bf136f157498c3b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ADB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> to be x. We want to find <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/3/4a3c570228283daae8c503d8a568832abcea73ca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ADE]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> - <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/d/56dc9127df69565a193a48d5172bbb711a5cef6e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle CDB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"73\" height=\"20\" />. So, that would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/3/e/e3e4da5c7be4b5400575b67e90b8b612276dfe95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle EBA]-[\\triangle ADB]=16-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"238\" height=\"20\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/3/5039fa49bda188964af85aadd1daa2bfb280eae2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ABC]-[\\triangle ADB]=12-x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"238\" height=\"20\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/f/8cf46f516957be0ea9bf464f152de7fb00b53829.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ADE]-[\\triangle DBC]=(16-x)-(12-x)=16-x-12+x= \\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"566\" height=\"32\" />\n</p><p>~ MathKatana\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/7/7/d77ee06209244e5b26cc40287c2ff258c1dad5a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE \\perp AB$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/9/be9cd94d70a9017b5e82095dca9d79f7430317f7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BC \\perp AB$\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/f/6/1f6d7514d189ebae6d583ba746c831c20e7e57ff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE \\parallel BC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"76\" height=\"19\" />. By alternate interior angles and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/8/a/38a32b1f092cd9dd7de4eccec461822ac0c5e76c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AA\\sim$\" width=\"46\" height=\"13\" />, we find that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a4722fcc2b4681bf03f14047dc5e4b6b55d532.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE \\sim \\triangle CDB$\" width=\"144\" height=\"13\" />, with side length ratio <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/b/3/7b33bd495b7492f95385da7afb197cd34638cdfa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{4}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"11\" height=\"37\" />. Their heights also have the same ratio, and since the two heights add up to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, we have that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/5/2/6521428d61f191fd653cae82d3ce10b5304e4a32.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{ADE} = 4 \\cdot \\frac{4}{7} = \\frac{16}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"37\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/5/6250ca9a39dbb313a10949d977f583524ceb1572.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$h_{CDB} = 3 \\cdot \\frac 47 = \\frac {12}7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"147\" height=\"37\" />. Subtracting the areas, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/3/00324b074de310d8cb3c8c6efca6904b43a95032.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 8 \\cdot \\frac {16}7 - \\frac 12 \\cdot 6 \\cdot \\frac{12}7 = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"196\" height=\"37\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/4/3/843622567e12d686e4e2f94ddfcb444e8ecde0d2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Rightarrow$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"9\" /> <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/9/1a9376a323ba22e23f0934e2eca624d5e7c32bd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"53\" height=\"29\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3\">Solution 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/3/f631f7a53d834de52b718ed6b496689e9658eadf.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[X]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"24\" height=\"18\" /> represent the area of figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/4/6a47ca0fe7cb276abc022af6ac88ddae1a9d6894.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$X$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />. Note that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf0f7f89e567669b122e8c013b4ca11e37dd631.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle BEA]=[\\triangle ABD]+[\\triangle ADE]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"253\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/6/086fd4bca85db5d287e525a878f3d9038f61c369.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle BCA]=[\\triangle ABD]+[\\triangle BDC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"254\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/1/2/e122ce5abe06381e17e2a1c78bd7f21bb086618f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ADE]-[\\triangle BDC]=[\\triangle BEA]-[\\triangle BCA]=\\frac{1}{2}\\times8\\times4-\\frac{1}{2}\\times6\\times4= 16-12=4\\Rightarrow\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"743\" height=\"37\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_4_.28coordbash.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4_(coordbash)\">Solution 4 (coordbash)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4 (coordbash)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Put figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/3/f13a96240c51d61ba3733d9f5c3020fa92ec4136.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABCDE$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"74\" height=\"14\" /> on a graph. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> goes from (0, 0) to (4, 6) and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> goes from (4, 0) to (0, 8). <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/5/12517bbc31cb9026c71299b7a0d232d07e60f284.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{AC}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"18\" /> is on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/8/2/782f5ce1864af21821f8311b7f9145ae10e0a4f8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = 1.5x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"67\" height=\"16\" />. <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/3/0f32db217d7630882c3441fa8821cd70a6958c3a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\overline{BE}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"31\" height=\"18\" /> is on line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/4/c/04cddcba43112b0a49b7e10209fbdcf3149da2b5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = -2x + 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"98\" height=\"16\" />. Finding intersection between these points,\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/5/f/45f7a890e91cad17c8b19cf92cd0062e30dd3604.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1.5x = -2x + 8$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"122\" height=\"14\" />. \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/f/d/6fd377a5c95e2bbfbb414b81c25dbce50b7fa06b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3.5x = 8$\" width=\"66\" height=\"12\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/c/c8c001bc84d380077acf3c707e023bd89823c33f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 8 \\times \\frac{2}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"77\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/e/2/4e2099770d2b536f7cc6f1df2dbdb24355592223.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{16}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"39\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>This gives us the x-coordinate of D. \nSo, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60a55b66cc723625ed1733eba83737d56ec2682f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> is the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />, then area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/0/db041d9c0fda44cf24b4f4ae7f02243ef2ea7f92.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADE$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" /> is \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/e/5ee101bc7bff99b1eb518e5a4c87c311157aee86.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{16}{7} \\times 8 \\times \\frac{1}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"87\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/c/1/9c15db2bc0753257ca4a0d99595b10941495c13a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$= \\frac{64}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"39\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Now, the height of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7a0327109ede54bf3abf9eb325bb58a503afc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/4/9/64959529658d302a4dd50385f57ecdd5dab88b29.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4-\\frac{16}{7} = \\frac{12}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"98\" height=\"37\" />\nAnd the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/7/1a7a0327109ede54bf3abf9eb325bb58a503afc2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BDC$\" width=\"60\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/7/d/77dbe07df0390a573b9358c1ec39362fb7ba816a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times \\frac{12}{7} \\times \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{36}{7}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"133\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>This gives us <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/8/d/08d262b06b05b0c270f1f2b4529ec24363cded8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{64}{7} - \\frac{36}{7} = 4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"100\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>Therefore, the difference is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_5\">Solution 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We want to figure out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/671dc24f33b16b3b423dffe34a34054169d5f489.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ADE] - [\\triangle BDC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"165\" height=\"20\" />.\nNotice that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c3a2d2224f7d163b46d702132425d47828bf538.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"61\" height=\"18\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/9/1598bab45a40d37f82c1c831ca6c67965a273d47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle BAE$\" width=\"58\" height=\"13\" /> \"intersect\" and form <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/8/e08af8f3acc34996e3cba566dc970b7ed496ba4b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADB$\" width=\"59\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>This means that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/5/9/059495d0ddaef8c5ec3575a5dc6f9ea8f5f1b8a5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle BAE] - [\\triangle ABC)] = [\\triangle ADE] - [\\triangle BDC]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"356\" height=\"20\" /> because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c42fa89302916d03f22d1bf136f157498c3b73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ADB]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"72\" height=\"20\" /> cancels out, which can be seen easily in the diagram.\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/a/50aa635df2f1f687bca49d352d0581ca7d437b60.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle BAE] = 0.5 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 8 = 16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"205\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/f/47f640bffee97f38ccf32ba23ae29e865be6b36f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle ABC] = 0.5 \\cdot 4 \\cdot 16 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"214\" height=\"20\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/6/416689a61b73741b4ba1286a1632420cfe37a2e5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[\\triangle BDC] - [\\triangle ADE] = 16 - 12 =\\boxed{\\mathrm{(B)}\\ 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"325\" height=\"32\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_6\">Solution 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Looking at the diagram, here are the following observations:\n</p>\n<pre>- Both have the same angles to the right and left of point D.\n- Line AE is perpendicular to AB, and so is BC perpendicular to AB, so AE and BC are parallel.\n- We see that triangle ADE is proportional, given that both widths are 4.\n</pre>\n<p>The area of triangle BAE - triangle ABC = 4, and triangle ABD cancels out. \nLeaving the answer, d = 4.\n</p><p>-By Thiagu Kannan\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution\">Video Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DlA71MBSviU\">https://youtu.be/DlA71MBSviU</a>\n</p><p>Education, the Study of Everything\n</p><p><br />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?t=131320\">AoPS topic</a></li></ul>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"2\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A\">2004 AMC 12A</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Answer_Key\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2004 AMC 12A Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2004_AMC_12A_Problems/Problem_9\" title=